%% Interactive toolset sign-in during a chat completion.
%% Separate from the OIDC login flow above (03-login-flow.mmd) — this is
%% DIAL Core asking the already-authenticated user to (re)supply toolset
%% credentials mid-completion via the client-channel RPC mechanism.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SPA as React SPA
    participant BFF as NestJS BFF
    participant CORE as DIAL Core

    SPA->>BFF: POST /api/v1/client-channel/subscribe
    BFF->>CORE: POST /v1/ops/client-channel/subscribe
    CORE-->>BFF: 200 text/event-stream<br/>X-DIAL-CLIENT-CHANNEL-ID: chan-1
    BFF-->>SPA: Relayed SSE stream<br/>X-DIAL-CLIENT-CHANNEL-ID: chan-1

    U->>SPA: Sends a chat message
    SPA->>BFF: POST /api/v1/conversations/completions<br/>{ clientChannelId: "chan-1", ... }
    BFF->>CORE: Completion request<br/>X-DIAL-CLIENT-CHANNEL-ID: chan-1

    CORE->>CORE: Tool call needs credentials
    CORE-->>BFF: SSE event on chan-1:<br/>{ id, method: "toolset/signin", params: { toolsetId } }
    BFF-->>SPA: Relayed SSE event

    SPA->>U: Shows global toolset sign-in dialog
    U->>SPA: Log in (API key or OAuth)
    SPA->>BFF: POST /api/v1/toolsets/{id}/login
    BFF->>CORE: POST /v1/ops/toolset/signin
    CORE-->>BFF: 200 success
    BFF-->>SPA: 200 success

    SPA->>BFF: POST /api/v1/client-channel/report<br/>{ id, result: "success" }
    BFF->>CORE: POST /v1/ops/client-channel/report
    CORE->>CORE: Resumes the blocked tool call
    CORE-->>BFF: Completion continues streaming
    BFF-->>SPA: Completion continues streaming

    Note over SPA,CORE: On logout, tab close, or the feature flag<br/>flipping off, the SPA unsubscribes the channel.
    SPA->>BFF: POST /api/v1/client-channel/unsubscribe
    BFF->>CORE: POST /v1/ops/client-channel/unsubscribe
